From ff2a108e10f71e637b8a247fe1a7832f6791c772 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 16:08:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] prose_portal: the desktop's environment for the commands it
 runs

A system job gets no environment from launch_daemon, which only sets
SAFEMODE; the desktop's PATH comes from SetupEnvironment, sourced by the
user session's jobs, and the portal is not one of them. A command run
through the portal therefore had no PATH at all (env showed none), so
`StyledEdit` was "command not found" while /boot/system/apps/StyledEdit
ran; it happened to resolve on the very first boot, where the package
was activated late. The job now sources SetupEnvironment the way
app_server's does, with HOME set to the home the desktop has.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0071-prose-portal-the-desktop-s-environment-for-the-commands-it-r.patch c79ea6f8ff86ed57b34472fd8485412b4ea338c1524cae0e474d5edce0908a7d
---
 data/launch/prose_portal | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/data/launch/prose_portal b/data/launch/prose_portal
index ba2cd3f20b..1f2033d27b 100644
--- a/data/launch/prose_portal
+++ b/data/launch/prose_portal
@@ -2,6 +2,14 @@
 # launch script, so the portal can be replaced on its own: a newer Prose drops
 # in a newer prose_portal.hpkg and need not bring a whole new system with it.
 service x-vnd.Haiku-prose_portal {
+	# A system job gets no environment from launch_daemon: the user session
+	# sources SetupEnvironment and this job never sees it, so a command run
+	# through the portal had no PATH and could not find /boot/system/apps.
+	# The desktop's environment, and the home the desktop has.
+	env {
+		from_script /system/boot/SetupEnvironment
+		HOME /boot/home
+	}
 	launch /system/servers/prose_portal
 	no_safemode
 	legacy
